"The normal form of the Section 10 Bayesian game, giving Player 1's expected payoff (Player 2
receives the negative). A strategy y<n><t> of Player 1 plays y<n> if Player 1 is in class a1 and
y<t> if in a2; a strategy z<u><v> of Player 2 plays z<u> if in b1 and z<v> if in b2. The only saddle
point is (y21,z21), with value 12.35.

The entry for (y11,z21) is printed as 11.20 and entered as printed, but the payoffs and
probabilities of the game imply 12.20; every other entry agrees with them."

